    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28043" root="عثكل" body-key="E">
    
      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَثْكَلَ الهَوْدَجَ</span></b> , (K, TA,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَثْكَلَةٌ</span>,
(TK,) <i>He adorned the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هودج</span> [or <i>women's camel-vehicle</i>] <i>with the kind of pendant termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُثْكُولَة</span>.
(K, * TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُثْكِلَ الهَوْدَجُ</span> <i>The</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هودج</span> <i>was</i> [<i>so</i>]
<i>adorned.</i> (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And [the inf. n.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَثْكَلَةٌ</span> signifies
<i>A heavy kind of running.</i> (K.) One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُعَثْكِلُ</span> <i>He runs heavily.</i> (TK.)

